-- Generated by drizzle-kit, then hand-amended for Phase 2 Slice 1.
-- BEFORE amendments (drizzle-kit output only):
--   CREATE TABLE profiles (... username check ...);
--   ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN user_id uuid;
--   CREATE UNIQUE INDEX profiles_username_unique ... WHERE username IS NOT NULL;
--   CREATE INDEX tasks_user_id_idx ON tasks (user_id);
--
-- Amendments add: auth.users FKs (no Auth-schema DDL), profiles/tasks RLS,
-- explicit privilege baselines (REVOKE ALL before every GRANT),
-- project-specific (lockdin_-prefixed) trigger/function names, an
-- updated_at trigger, a handle_new_user trigger, and an Auth-user profile
-- backfill.
--
-- Stop 2 correction (this revision):
--   - Renamed public.handle_new_user / public.set_profiles_updated_at and
--     their triggers to lockdin_-prefixed names. Generic/hosted Auth
--     objects are never touched by this migration.
--   - Switched CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION -> CREATE FUNCTION for both
--     functions: a name collision on first apply must fail the migration
--     loudly, not silently overwrite something already on the project.
--   - Removed every DROP TRIGGER statement, including the previous
--     (incorrect) "DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS on_auth_user_created ON
--     auth.users" — this migration must never drop anything on auth.users,
--     under any name.
--   - Added explicit REVOKE ALL PRIVILEGES on profiles / tasks /
--     tasks_id_seq before granting back only the exact intended access,
--     instead of relying on default/table-level grants.
--   - Added REVOKE ... FROM PUBLIC/anon/authenticated for
--     lockdin_set_profiles_updated_at() (previously only handle_new_user
--     had these revokes).
--   - Normalised full_name metadata extraction so blank strings are treated
--     as absent (NULLIF(BTRIM(...), '')), not stored as empty text, in both
--     the signup trigger and the existing-user backfill.
--
-- Final Stop 2 evidence/hardening pass (this revision):
--   - Added REVOKE ALL PRIVILEGES ... FROM PUBLIC as a separate statement
--     preceding every anon/authenticated REVOKE on profiles, tasks, and
--     tasks_id_seq. Revoking from PUBLIC matters independently: any role
--     (including future roles) inherits whatever PUBLIC is granted, so a
--     stray PUBLIC grant would silently defeat the anon/authenticated
--     REVOKEs below it.
--
-- Do NOT apply until Stop 2 approval. Do NOT set tasks.user_id NOT NULL
-- until the hosted task-row audit
-- (docs/sql/phase2/phase2-pre-migration-audit.sql) decides wipe vs backfill.

